{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor actively queried the workspace for records, elicited critical wound and glucose red flags, recognized bone cement detachment plus poor healing as requiring urgent in-person assessment, gave safe insulin/metformin guidance without inventing doses, directed the family to emergency with a concrete plan and obtained caregiver read-back. No responsibility-chain item was missed or seriously erred; minor RC4 omission (not explicitly naming missing cultures/labs) does not create a safety error, and all five dimensions are at least good. Two high-order points (HO2 dynamic reprioritization and HO3 safe bounded closure) were triggered and completed with meaningful impact, while HO1 and HO4 were not fully completed. Closure is safe, executable, and traceable as valid_closure.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00074",
        "explanation": "Doctor gives concrete next-step plan with destination, timing, and backup path.",
        "quote": "先到急诊分诊台，完整说明：“糖尿病足术后一个多月，右脚伤口近期更红、有异味和黄色渗液，今天骨水泥脱出，食欲差，血糖19点几，晚饭未正常吃，餐前胰岛素、晚间胰岛素和二甲双胍今晚尚未使用，药物实物都带来了。”"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00091",
        "explanation": "Caregiver confirms arrival at emergency, execution of plan, and that medication and records were brought.",
        "quote": "我们已经到原来医院急诊分诊台这边了，没有等明天。"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The doctor translated risk into a concrete plan with specific destination (emergency triage), timing (tonight, not waiting), materials to bring (records, insulin pens, medications), and a backup escalation pathway (call 120 if deterioration). The caregiver confirmed execution by arriving at the emergency department and following the triage script. Closure is safe and traceable.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
